prompt:
You are given a vulnerability brief and the affected source file(s) from a Python repository at the vulnerable revision. Produce a patch that fixes the vulnerability class described, while keeping legitimate behaviour working. Respond with a single unified diff (git format, paths relative to the repository root) and no other text.

## Vulnerability brief

Vulnerability class: path traversal (CWE-22) in static file serving.

A static resource handler resolves the requested file path against
its root directory. When the resource is configured to follow
symlinks, the containment check that verifies the resolved file stays
inside the root directory is skipped entirely, so a request path with
parent-directory segments (including percent-encoded forms, which the
server decodes before dispatch) reads files outside the root.

Affected area: aiohttp/web_urldispatcher.py (static resource request
handling). The snapshot is the last vulnerable revision. Produce a
source patch that keeps resolved paths contained even when symlink
following is enabled, while keeping legitimate static serving and
intentional symlink access working.

## Affected file: aiohttp/web_urldispatcher.py

