## Vulnerability brief

Vulnerability class: path traversal (CWE-22) in static resource
routing.

A static resource decides whether a request belongs to it by testing
the raw request path against its URL prefix. The path is not
normalised first, so a path that begins with the prefix but contains
dot segments escaping it still resolves to the resource, even though
the normalised path is outside the prefix (and can be outside the
served root). This lets crafted paths probe and reach filesystem
locations the routing was supposed to exclude. For example, the
request path /st/../secret.txt begins with the /st prefix but
normalises to a location outside it.

Affected area: aiohttp/web_urldispatcher.py (static resource
resolution). The snapshot is the last vulnerable revision. Produce a
source patch that normalises the path before the prefix decision,
while keeping legitimate static routing working.

